{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/600616-mortal-remains-gmc-update-faq","id":600616,"title":"Mortal Remains GMC Update - FAQ","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-23T09:40:18-07:00","id":600616,"title":"Mortal Remains GMC Update - FAQ","content":"Collective topic for the questions on mechanic patch in <b>Mortal Remains</b>. I feel to ask some question as we started a Hunter chronicle ( in that I <i>play</i>, not run, at last! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and some problems with understanding a rules come up. I also hope this topic help to polish some mechanics for proper Hunter 2ED in future. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> First question - <b>Practical Beats are still earn for the whole cell?</b> Even if character sheets and text is mentioning them as Blood or Arcane Experience, in the way the solo characters earn them, not the group as whole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T09:50:58-07:00","id":600643,"title":"","content":"Second topic - Encountering supernatural is in <b>God Machine Chronicle</b> a Breaking Point on Integrity. <b>Mortal Remains Patch</b> mentions that killing supernatural is still a Breaking Point for hunters. <b>Does this mean our hunters roll their Resolve + Composure each time they see something supernatural?</b> Even a minor thing like a Manifested ghost that do not do any harm to them, only is &quot;otherworldly&quot;? <b>Also, would Abjurations of the ephemeral being be also Breaking Point, even if characters knows it does not &quot;kill&quot; the being?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T10:29:53-07:00","id":600705,"title":"","content":"The former seems like a yes. It's pretty spooky after all. If you're feeling generous/don't feel it's particularly worth focusing on, you might make ir one with a +1 bonus or something, but avoiding it denies the easy opportunity to give your players Spooked to incentivize them to do something dumb and awesome and make story happen.<br /> <br /> The latter? Probably not. Or if it is, it's not the same as killing somebody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T10:43:36-07:00","id":600716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/600616-mortal-remains-gmc-update-faq?p=600705#post600705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The former seems like a yes. It's pretty spooky after all. If you're feeling generous/don't feel it's particularly worth focusing on, you might make ir one with a +1 bonus or something, but avoiding it denies the easy opportunity to give your players Spooked to incentivize them to do something dumb and awesome and make story happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then <b>each encounter</b> with Enemy could lead to Integrity loss - and that mean that characters will lost one Integrity per session ( if one session is like 4-5 encounters with monsters ). That makes hunters unplayable after 8 session chronicle - from Integrity 7 to Integrity 0... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/600616-mortal-remains-gmc-update-faq?p=600705#post600705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter? Probably not. Or if it is, it's not the same as killing somebody.</div> </div> </div> </div> No roll at all for using Abjurations on Integrity then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-24-2015, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T12:52:12-07:00","id":600851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/600616-mortal-remains-gmc-update-faq?p=600643#post600643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second topic - Encountering supernatural is in <b>God Machine Chronicle</b> a Breaking Point on Integrity. <b>Mortal Remains Patch</b> mentions that killing supernatural is still a Breaking Point for hunters. <b>Does this mean our hunters roll their Resolve + Composure each time they see something supernatural?</b> Even a minor thing like a Manifested ghost that do not do any harm to them, only is &quot;otherworldly&quot;? <b>Also, would Abjurations of the ephemeral being be also Breaking Point, even if characters knows it does not &quot;kill&quot; the being?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The keystone of the new Integrity system is to use common sense to decide whether an event is traumatic or not. Integrity is relative to an extent, and a hardened veteran of the Vigil ought not to be shocked every time he encounters something new and paranormal. Killing a supernatural being is a breaking point not because it's supernatural but because it's murder; it's a psychological shock to feel the knife in your hand and do the deed yourself. I don't think an abjuration would have the same kind of visceral shock that murder does, as the nature of the ritual highlights that you're doing something that is not quite the same as tearing a body apart. An especially traumatic and powerful abjuration might constitute a breaking point, depending on how terrible a display of power the ephemera resists with.<br /> <br /> So: use your judgment (or your Storyteller's judgment). A breaking point is a traumatic shock. A rookie member of the Union might be shocked just to witness his first werewolf or vampire. A veteran who's seen friends die on the field probably isn't going to be shocked by the paranormal short of witnessing the face of God or an impossible Abyssal horror, something unknowable and powerful, but if he's cracking human-like skulls open with a lead pipe every night, that's still going to take its toll on him.<br /> <br /> Losing Integrity isn't as severe in consequences as losing Morality was in 1e. I don't believe it's an iron-clad rule that characters who lose their last dot of Integrity become unplayable, and the results of most failed Integrity checks are less severe than gaining a derangement in the old system. Its biggest effects, I think, are indirect results \u2014 a weakened spirit leaves you less prepared to resist or exert certain effects, as represented by stuff that rolls Integrity as a dice pool, or if your soul is stripped from you, you're dangerously close to being broken quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T14:32:22-07:00","id":600976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/600616-mortal-remains-gmc-update-faq?p=600716#post600716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then <b>each encounter</b> with Enemy could lead to Integrity loss - and that mean that characters will lost one Integrityper session ( if one session is like 4-5 encounters with monsters ). That makes hunters unplayable after 8 session chronicle - from Integrity 7 to Integrity 0... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>My experience with Integrity 7 people going after the supernatural with tiny (0 or -1) breaking points when they initially witness a new thing hasn't really lead to the kind of data you're assuming, so I'm not sure where you're getting this from.<br /> <br /> It's like how assuming that just because a vampire has to roll Humanity means they're likely to lose it. Rolling for it doesn't usually mean losing it, especially when you've got an average of 5 dice on the roll.<br /> <br /> It <i>does </i>make certain they'll have the Spooked or Shaken Condition, which can prompt them to do more <i>interesting </i>things in hopes of resolving for a beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T00:38:12-07:00","id":601454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/600616-mortal-remains-gmc-update-faq?p=600716#post600716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then <b>each encounter</b> with Enemy could lead to Integrity loss - and that mean that characters will lost one Integrityper session ( if one session is like 4-5 encounters with monsters ). That makes hunters unplayable after 8 session chronicle - from Integrity 7 to Integrity 0... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There is no integrity 0, the scale is 1-10. Humans never become unplayable from losing Integrity in GMC.<br /> At Integrity 1 it's just more likely to get a dramatic failure on your Breaking Point roll, but even if you get the maximum penalty to your roll a base Resolve+Composure of 6+ will make sure you'll never involuntarily suffer a dramatic failure on that roll.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T01:00:48-07:00","id":601458,"title":"","content":"Okay, so rolls should be made for <b>ALL</b> supernatural encounters, at least on begining of characters Vigil. ( Probably one roll for each first encouter )<br /> <br /> <b>But how Practical Expiriance works?</b> On Mr. Gone Sheets there is section for individual Pools of them. It's wierd that text mentions it like whole group is taking them in one pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}